    {'heading': 'Lesson XXVII'},
    {'para': '**285. Demonstrative Pronouns.** Two demonstrative-declensions are made up with particular irregularity: they are those of the pronouns ⟨ayam⟩ and ⟨asau⟩ (for which the natives give the stem-forms as ⟨idam⟩ and ⟨adas⟩ respectively). The first is a more indefinite demonstrative: ‘this’ or ‘that’; the other signifies especially the remoter relation.'},
    {'para': '**286.** ⟨ayam⟩ (⟨idam⟩):'},
    {'table': {'head': ['Masculine', 'Sing.', 'Dual', 'Plural', 'Fem. Sing.', 'Fem. Dual', 'Fem. Plural'], 'rows': [['N.', '⟨ayam⟩', '⟨imau⟩', '⟨ime⟩', '⟨iyam⟩', '⟨ime⟩', '⟨imās⟩'], ['A.', '⟨imam⟩', '„', '⟨imān⟩', '⟨imām⟩', '„', '„'], ['I.', '⟨anena⟩', '⟨ābhyām⟩', '⟨ebhis⟩', '⟨anayā⟩', '⟨ābhyām⟩', '⟨ābhis⟩'], ['D.', '⟨asmai⟩', '„', '⟨ebhyas⟩', '⟨asyai⟩', '„', '⟨ābhyas⟩'], ['Ab.', '⟨asmāt⟩', '„', '„', '⟨asyās⟩', '„', '„'], ['G.', '⟨asya⟩', '⟨anayos⟩', '⟨eṣām⟩', '„', '⟨anayos⟩', '⟨āsām⟩'], ['L.', '⟨asmin⟩', '„', '⟨eṣu⟩', '⟨asyām⟩', '„', '⟨āsu⟩']]}},
